---
source: crates/solar-cli/tests/snapshots_of_the_screen.rs
expression: "screen(&[\"--help\"])"
---
SOLAR speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 over standard input and output, one message per line. `solar call` prints the whole envelope, which is what any other interface would receive; the other commands are the same APIs with their output laid out for a person.

The contract is docs/CONTRACT.md and the errors are docs/ERRORS.md.

Usage: solar.exe [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  call      Run one call and print the whole response envelope
  serve     Answer requests on standard input until it ends, one JSON message per line
  list      List every API this build answers to
  describe  Describe one API, with its parameters, its errors and its examples
  manifest  Print the manifest
  version   Print the version of SOLAR and how this binary was built
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Indent the JSON that goes to standard output

      --log <LEVEL>
          Diagnostics on standard error: off, error, warn, info, debug or trace

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes: 0 success, 2 invalid argument, 3 not found, 5 failed precondition, 8 deadline exceeded, 9 unavailable, 10 unimplemented, 11 internal. The whole table is in docs/CONTRACT.md.
